{"seq": 0, "t": "2026-11-06T14:28:15.531Z", "kind": "job.submit", "payload": {"job_id": "57", "type": "train", "spec": {"steps": 20, "lr": 2e-05, "batch": 8, "seed_start": 815000, "reward": "…/20261105T135924_3394386/reward_grpo_rev2_062813.py", "init": "…/adapters/grpo_rev", "start_preset": null, "start_mix": null, "note": "Use exactly this and make the placement robust. (1) plan_grasp the green cube; move the end-effector to that grasp pose with its full orientation, close, lift 0.2m. (2) Take a FRESH observation; estimate the grasped green cube center by backprojecting its mask to 3D and, before the oriented bounding box, KEEP ONLY points within 0.07 m of the median point height (the SAM mask can contain stray non-cube pixels; the lifted cube is isolated so its mask is clean); the cube is rigidly held by the gripper, so this center is accurate. (3) offset = grasped_center - current_end_effector_position. (4) place_z = red_center_z + red_half_z + green_half_z; move the end-effector to (red_center_x - offset_x, red_center_y - offset_y, place_z - offset_z) so the CUBE center lands on the red cube center (NEVER move the end-effector to the red cube center directly; the cube is held at a fixed offset from it). (5) move there at a safe height, descend, place, open. Re-estimating the grasped center from the lifted observation and rejecting stray pixels is what makes it succeed on every seed.", "goal": null, "time": "07:05:00", "name": "grpo_rev2", "task": "revstack", "rollouts": 8, "stop_when": {"plateau_steps": 8, "min_gain": 0.01}, "train_defaults": {"defaults": "identity-v2", "defaulted": []}}, "slurm_jobs": ["42996633"], "policy_model": "Qwen3.8-27B"}, "files": []}
